//!
//! # Port-Mapped I/O
//!
//! The `in` and `out` instructions, the only way to reach devices that live in
//! the x86 I/O port space.
//!
//! ## Overview
//!
//! Besides the memory address space, x86 has a separate I/O port space. It
//! has 65536 ports (`0x0000` to `0xFFFF`), each holding one byte, and is
//! reached only with `in` and `out`. Both instructions are privileged: in
//! ring 3 they raise a general protection fault (`#GP`) unless the TSS I/O
//! permission bitmap allows the port, and IgniOS has no such bitmap. Port
//! accesses are never cached.
//!
//! The ports this kernel uses:
//!
//! | Ports                    | Device                                      | File                 |
//! |--------------------------|---------------------------------------------|----------------------|
//! | `0x20-0x21`, `0xA0-0xA1` | 8259 PIC pair                               | `pic.ign`            |
//! | `0x3F8-0x3FD`            | COM1 16550 UART                             | `drivers/serial.ign` |
//! | `0x42-0x43`, `0x61`      | PIT channel 2                               | `pit.ign`            |
//! | `0x60`, `0x64`           | 8042 PS/2 controller                        | `drivers/ps2.ign`    |
//! | `0x80`                   | POST diagnostic port, used as a short delay | `pic.ign`            |
//!
//! Inline `asm` blocks are opaque to the optimizer, so the compiler neither
//! drops nor reorders these accesses and no `volatile` qualifier is needed.
//! See concept doc 06.

/// Namespace for the byte-wide port instructions.
namespace Arch::Port {
  /// Reads one byte from `port` (`in al, dx`). The port number travels in DX,
  /// which is why the operand is a register and not an immediate: an immediate
  /// port is limited to `0x00-0xFF`.
  function readByte(port: u16): u8 {
    return asm (port in dx) -> (value: u8 in al) { in {value}, {port} };
  }

  /// Writes `value` to `port` (`out dx, al`).
  function writeByte(port: u16, value: u8): void {
    asm (port in dx, value in al) { out {port}, {value} }
  }
}
